WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.223 --> 00:00:02.820
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.930
- Hi, I'm Preeti Mistry.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.580
I'm a chef, author, and activist.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.140
And today I'm going to be taste testing

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.150
some grocery store, instant Indian meals.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.120
The thing I love the most

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.960
about Indian food is the
pow of the different spices.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.910
Like, I'm a Libra,

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.030
and so balance is really important to me.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.710
When I'm making a masala

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.148
I'm thinking about the sweet, salty,

00:00:22.148 --> 00:00:23.420
spicy,

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.570
tangy,

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.403
et cetera.

00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:28.890
There is a fine balance when
it all works, that just evens

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.510
out all of those different
sort of powerful flavors

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.233
Nice and chunky.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.940
For how tangy it,

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:38.980
the aroma is,

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.610
I'm expecting more sort of acid,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.443
but it's actually just

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.850
kind of creamy and spicy
for like, you know, middle

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.100
of the road, Indian restaurant.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.460
I don't think you would get
anything that much better

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.293
than this.

00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:52.520
I feel like, you know, I
would want to add a little

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.930
more salt and lemon juice,
maybe some fresh cilantro.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:00.160
I think out of five stars, I
would give this dahl probably

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.980
three and a quarter three and a half.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.330
I feel like this is something
I could add a little bit

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.180
more spice to and a little
more salt and lemon juice,

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.313
and I would be perfectly
happy with it, quite honestly.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.060
It looks

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.160
like a chicken curry I would
get like in an airplane.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.883
Let's go rice and sauce
first, just to kind of get a.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:29.630
Rice is very sticky, a little
mushy kind of textureless.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.958
The only spice I really
get is black pepper.

00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:36.960
The texture of the chicken
is very, it's not tough.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.560
It's a little stringy.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.390
I don't really get any
Indian flavor at all.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.990
It's just kind of tastes like

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.060
braised chicken in tomato sauce.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.390
I would give this half a star.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.740
Texturally, it's challenged,

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.950
boiled chicken, sticky,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.300
kind of mushy rice.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.850
It definitely needs salt and acid

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.350
but it also needs just some sort

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.920
of nuanced spice to think
like, if I close my eyes

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.800
and somebody gave this
to me and told me it was

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.393
like some Italian chicken,
I'd be like, okay.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.420
Full disclosure, I have met
Sukhi and her whole family.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.020
They're very nice people.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.420
I am excited to try this

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.730
because I love samosas,
who doesn't love samosas?

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:17.563
Look at that.

00:02:17.563 --> 00:02:18.460
It's crispy.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:19.850
Ooh. Look at brown.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:20.683
Let's see here.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.520
The pastry is quite good.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.550
The interior so far, I
get more nuanced spice

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.430
but it still feels like
it's lacking in salt

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.280
but let's maybe try dipping it

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.173
in the chutney and see if
that helps with the salt.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.130
I feel like someone who

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.920
is spice averse would probably love this.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.430
I would give the chicken
tikka masala samosas

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.250
two and a quarter stars.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.650
I'm really wanting more salt
and spice, but texture's great.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.740
The pastry is fantastic.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.540
I feel like I want more,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.373
pow.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.890
All right. Hmm. It
actually smells quite good.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.680
This is also Sukhi's

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.430
but this is chicken tikka
masala with naan bread,

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.040
it's called on the box,
which is redundant.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.980
But I understand trying
to meet your customer

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.813
where they're at.

00:03:13.813 --> 00:03:16.563
Let's see, I don't want to burn my tongue.

00:03:21.485 --> 00:03:25.470
The flavor, you get a
lot of clove, cinnamon.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.450
Definitely the fenugreek, ginger.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.170
I would say the biggest issue
I have right now is just

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.680
that it really needs more salt.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.780
Let's try some rice.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:35.180
Now, the rice also, I'll
give you a look at that.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.020
It looks a lot more like separate grains

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:42.110
as opposed to the Signature
Select that sorta look

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.113
like kind of mushy sticky.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.640
Texturally, so far,

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.110
I feel like this is the
best thing we've had.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.250
Let's try the naan, again, it's got

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.870
some nice browning on the
back there you can see.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:55.810
I love naan.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.460
Now bread in a microwave
is going to be chewy.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.230
So there's nothing crispy about this.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.550
Like a regular naan that
you get out of a tandoor.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.660
It'd be like crisp on the edges and soft.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.950
This is a little bit
more like soft and chewy.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.057
Just gotta get the.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.493
Chewy.

00:04:14.493 --> 00:04:16.230
If I got this naan in here,

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.013
I would just throw it in the toaster.

00:04:18.013 --> 00:04:20.270
I think I would give this one

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:24.160
because of the lack of salt and spice

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.310
I'm going to go three and a half.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:29.140
The variety of starches,
the bread and the rice.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.100
I think it was a bonus.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.290
If you were to toast the naan

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.821
I think you'd get probably
the best sort of, you know

00:04:35.821 --> 00:04:38.410
grocery store naan experience.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.590
And the curry just needs
to be boosted a little bit.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.700
I think if you are buying
these meals and you like them

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.640
and you want to go a little
bit deeper in your enjoyment

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.350
or appreciation or
understanding of Indian cuisine

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.890
I would definitely say go to
your local Indian restaurant.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.650
Because even if it's mediocre

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:00.260
it's probably going to be 10
times better than anything

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:01.288
I just tasted.

00:05:01.288 --> 00:05:03.871
(upbeat music)

